8x04|n|To consider by turning a subject in the mind, and viewing it in its different aspects and relations; to meditate; to contemplate; to theorize; as, to speculate on questions in religion; to speculate on political events. ; To view subjects from certain premises given or assumed, and infer conclusions respecting them a priori. ; To purchase with the expectation of a contingent advance in value, and a consequent sale at a profit; -- often, in a somewhat depreciative sense, of unsound or hazardous transactions; as, to speculate in coffee, in sugar, or in bank stock. ; To consider attentively; as, to speculate the nature of a thing.	a:3j42,11,22~3j42,11,22	v:24mb,23,1~24mb,23,1	n:3sp6,15,3~3sp6,15,3
