8xp8|n|A slender stalk or blade in vegetation; as, a spire grass or of wheat. ; A tapering body that shoots up or out to a point in a conical or pyramidal form. Specifically (Arch.), the roof of a tower when of a pyramidal form and high in proportion to its width; also, the pyramidal or aspiring termination of a tower which can not be said to have a roof, such as that of Strasburg cathedral; the tapering part of a steeple, or the steeple itself. ; A tube or fuse for communicating fire to the chargen in blasting. ; The top, or uppermost point, of anything; the summit. ; A spiral; a curl; a whorl; a twist. ; The part of a spiral generated in one revolution of the straight line about the pole. See Spiral, n.	a:874z,125,8;1rss,106,5;70et,104,2;1bkx,102,2;2ugb,91,1;8ps5,91,1;9x77,88,2;9e19,68,3;1ztn,65,5;1d78,59,8;4j9g,30,2;3uj8,21,1;3uh4,19,1;ys5,12,1~874z,125,8;1d78,59,8;1ztn,65,5;1rss,106,5;9e19,68,3;70et,104,2;9x77,88,2;4j9g,30,2;1bkx,102,2;3uh4,19,1;8ps5,91,1;3uj8,21,1;2ugb,91,1;ys5,12,1	v:84wq,70,8;a2ek,50,2;4j9g,36,3;a7g2,27,66;a6d9,8,23;a6ev,6,6~a7g2,27,66;a6d9,8,23;84wq,70,8;a6ev,6,6;4j9g,36,3;a2ek,50,2	V:7xsm,50,5;4j8a,14,2~7xsm,50,5;4j8a,14,2	n:ywf,155,10;2ugb,132,17;874z,115,4;8ps5,114,5;82oz,109,8;8ot4,95,28;9x77,88,2;1ick,84,24;93jo,70,7;83o1,63,4;4qyq,61,1;ys5,38,6;4j9g,36,3;3uh4,29,2;173f,18,15~8ot4,95,28;1ick,84,24;2ugb,132,17;173f,18,15;598y,4,15;ywf,155,10;82oz,109,8;93jo,70,7;ys5,38,6;8ps5,114,5;83o1,63,4;874z,115,4;1u12,16,3;4j9g,36,3;3uh4,29,2	N:29if,97,6;8xhy,85,6;6ev0,69,9;akwo,61,6;57fs,45,22;ajvx,45,3;6zc7,39,4;3rdn,21,2~57fs,45,22;6ev0,69,9;29if,97,6;akwo,61,6;8xhy,85,6;6zc7,39,4;ajvx,45,3;3rdn,21,2
